{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>Arise, O YHWH.</b> After the manner of men, who stand to do battle:" "And the meaning of <b>and let them scatter</b> — when they see that You have arisen to make war, immediately Your enemies will scatter:" "The word <b>Your foes</b> [משנאיך] is from the heavy [i.e., hitpa'el] binyan, and the nun is light to lighten for the tongue:" "<b>And let them scatter and flee.</b> After the manner of all prophecies, to double with variant words, as I will explain in the pericope of Balaam:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:05.224679728Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}